# --- SIGNING ---
#
# The release signing key and its passwords. app/build.gradle.kts reads jks.properties
# when it exists and falls back to environment variables in CI, so a fresh clone builds
# unsigned rather than failing — which means nothing here needs to be committed for the
# project to work, and committing any of it would hand over the ability to publish an
# APK Android accepts as an update to a real user's install.
#
# *.jks is the backstop for the several names a keystore gets given by accident.
jks.properties
release.jks
*.jks
*.keystore
google-play-api.json

# --- BUILD OUTPUTS ---
#
# /build is already ignored above, but AGP also writes the copy-to-release-directory
# output here when a release build runs locally, and the repository currently has an
# APK, its output-metadata.json and a baseline profile committed under this path from
# before it was ignored. Those are build products: they cannot be reviewed, they go
# stale silently, and a checked-in APK invites someone to install a build nobody can
# trace to a commit. Releases are the place for an APK.
#
# NOTE: those existing files are still TRACKED. A .gitignore entry does not untrack
# anything, so this rule only stops NEW ones appearing. Removing them is a separate,
# deliberate commit — `git rm -r --cached app/release/` — left out of this change so
# that deleting four files from history-going-forward is its own reviewable decision.
/app/release/
/app/debug/
/dist/
